# Article source Markdown.
#
# These live in the repo root for authoring convenience, but the repo root IS
# the Cloudflare Pages publish root: anything committed here is served. A
# committed article source would be reachable at /<slug>.md and would be a
# full duplicate of the published article, which Google can index and treat
# as competing content.
#
# Keeping them untracked means they never reach Cloudflare (Pages deploys the
# cloned repo, not your working tree) while staying available locally.
/*.md
!/README.md
